eld" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${T}_{1}$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u-1 \\\\ {e}^{v}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v)\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the exponential term ${e}^{v}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v \\\\ u-2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the term $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f878c5d873ff6311da3dc9245bc02e778b68b66ad92843dae863dbce586c6dbd" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only"] "category" "ma_