3 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=4v-u,\\,y=3v-7\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4v-u \\\\ 3v-7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4v-u \\\\ 3v-7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+4v \\\\ 3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-1+4+0=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f878c5d873ff6311da3dc9245bc02e778b68b66ad92843dae863dbce586c6dbd" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "723a3905b77c613d5d439d20eb56e456d44fea25808fdc171fc24134857c48b2" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]$\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]$\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/example-9505.json" "file_sha256" "a86f53ae940196ebcb6a9d659d66c981838147b2d7c8d240d6eee16099a28771" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_1$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_1$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ v-2u+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ -2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_2$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ -u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_3$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic term $v^2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$\\mathbf{T}_1$ and $\\mathbf{T}_2$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/example-9505.json" "file_sha256" "a86f53ae940196ebcb6a9d659d66c981838147b2d7c8d240d6eee16099a28771" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 3u-v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{a}, \\qquad y = u + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{b}v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{c}\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/example-9508.json" "file_sha256" "e0667a9efd2b05d09a4f2e32b32e1102fb78daf5f51fc9bf04bb7a55b7e42a83" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v \\\\ u-5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v+1 \\\\ u-5v\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = 3u - v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{1}, \\qquad y = u + (\\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{-5})v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{0} \\, .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+(-5)+0 = -4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/example-9508.json" "file_sha256" "e0667a9efd2b05d09a4f2e32b32e1102fb78daf5f51fc9bf04bb7a55b7e42a83" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 5u + v - 6, \\qquad y = 2u + 4v\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/example-9506.json" "file_sha256" "063600f9abe5c5578be06f245958b40419fee0fc3a7f0ebf1b3953a6bf833f4f" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-9506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v-6 \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+2+0 = 3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/example-9506.json" "file_sha256" "063600f9abe5c5578be06f245958b40419fee0fc3a7f0ebf1b3953a6bf833f4f" "basis" 1243 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-124245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}7u-v+6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}8v-9u \\\\ 4u-v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u-5 \\\\ 8u\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7u-v+6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7u-v \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8v-9u \\\\ 4u-v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9u+8v \\\\ 4u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-5 \\\\ 8u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ 8u\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}.$\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "91e829927bb4b43e9dc8ec971249eec069d44acd93ffdea064ddc99b18a1ff39"} {"question" "q-124245" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124245" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124245" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}v-6u+7 \\\\ 4u+3v-5\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2u+v \\\\ uv+1\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-6u+7 \\\\ 4u+3v-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6u+v \\\\ 4u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124237" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "91e829927bb4b43e9dc8ec971249eec069d44acd93ffdea064ddc99b18a1ff39"} {"question" "q-124237" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124237" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124237" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ 1-{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u(v-1) \\\\ u-1\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}9 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{1}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cubic term ${v}^{3}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "91e829927bb4b43e9dc8ec971249eec069d44acd93ffdea064ddc99b18a1ff39"} {"question" "q-124247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{3}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${T}_{1}$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u-1 \\\\ {e}^{v}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v)\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the exponential term ${e}^{v}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v \\\\ u-2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the term $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "91e829927bb4b43e9dc8ec971249eec069d44acd93ffdea064ddc99b18a1ff39"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{3}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${T}_{2}$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}v-7u+3 \\\\ 3v-u+1\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}uv+1 \\\\ u-2v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-7u+3 \\\\ 3v-u+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7u+v \\\\ -u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{3}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "91e829927bb4b43e9dc8ec971249eec069d44acd93ffdea064ddc99b18a1ff39"} {"question" "q-124255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au-2v+b,\\,y=4u+cv-2\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6u-2v \\\\ 4u+7v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6u-2v+1 \\\\ 4u+7v-2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-6u-2v+1,\\,y=4u+7v-2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-6+1+7=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "91e829927bb4b43e9dc8ec971249eec069d44acd93ffdea064ddc99b18a1ff39"} {"question" "q-124267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+bv+3,\\,y=-9u+cv+4\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ -9u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+3 \\\\ -9u+4v+4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=1u+0v+3,\\,y=-9u+4v+4\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+0+4=5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home