nd $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+6v \\\\ 3u-4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+6v \\\\ 3u-4v\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=1u+6v+0,\\,y=3u-4v\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+0+3=4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "91e829927bb4b43e9dc8ec971249eec069d44acd93ffdea064ddc99b18a1ff39"} {"question" "q-124265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124265" "field" "