question" "q-124091" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+4v \\\\ 2u-5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+4v+2 \\\\ 2u-5v+1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-u+4v+2,\\,y=2u-5v+1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=4+2+1=7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124091" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "91e829927bb4b43e9dc8ec971249eec069d44acd93ffdea064ddc99b18a1ff39"} {"question" "q-124091" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124091" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124091" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=5u-3v-2,\\,y=2u+v+7\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ a & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v-2 \\\\ 2u+v+7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v-2 \\\\ 2u+v+7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+1+(-2)=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "91e829927bb4b43e9dc8ec971249eec069d44acd93ffdea064ddc99b18a1ff39"} {"question" "q-124285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=-5v-2,\\,y=7v-2u-3\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ -2 & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5v-2 \\\\ 7v-2u-3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5v-2 \\\\ 7v-2u-3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5v \\\\ -2u+7v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-5+7+(-2)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "91e829927bb4b43e9dc8ec971249eec069d44acd93ffdea064ddc99b18a1ff39"} {"question" "q-124295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-7"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=5u+3,\\,y=7v-u\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ b & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5u+3 \\\\ 7v-u\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+3 \\\\ 7v-u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u \\\\ -u+7v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=5+(-1)+3=7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "91e829927bb4b43e9dc8ec971249eec069d44acd93ffdea064ddc99b18a1ff39"} {"question" "q-124291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=6u-v,\\,y=2u-3v+4\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & -1 \\\\ 2 & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v+4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=6+(-3)+4=7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "91e829927bb4b43e9dc8ec971249eec069d44acd93ffdea064ddc99b18a1ff39"} {"question" "q-124301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "13"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=4v-u,\\,y=3v-7\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4v-u \\\\ 3v-7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4v-u \\\\ 3v-7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+4v \\\\ 3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-1+4+0=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "91e829927bb4b43e9dc8ec971249eec069d44acd93ffdea064ddc99b18a1ff39"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "q-124284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/state.json" "file_sha256" "48add56246250d5c8e0bbf656b624667b997c1353c3aa845ed04e7180594fe69"} {"question" "e-9505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/3a24d08f3fce05b0a69b361d96cde0766860e0fd466a2622d780572334b2deba.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/d910373a10dd1d08aed3df8b6b40102f4f1cc42e94e099ba6c74e6c5065828a1.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/05831230ea1993c0df5f2dae6d6411da094f181006980ea261a5b55fc9f21b40.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/example-9505.json" "file_sha256" "915b63ba37be51133fd667e5635dacc63803664f80a1d9f9709fca076564787e"} {"question" "e-9505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_1$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_1$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ v-2u+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ -2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_2$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ -u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_3$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic term $v^2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$\\mathbf{T}_1$ and $\\mathbf{T}_2$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/example-9505.json" "file_sha256" "915b63ba37be51133fd667e5635dacc63803664f80a1d9f9709fca076564787e"} {"question" "e-9508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 3u-v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{a}, \\qquad y = u + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{b}v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{c}\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/43bcde1806155410ba97b0b2e5807d4a0f9cee93ef04f2ccfb413552de74178b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/example-9508.json" "file_sha256" "03e56da4988b3c55d6fa51e8dc7baa835203339981eb89c541877bebc4fbad27"} {"question" "e-9508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v \\\\ u-5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v+1 \\\\ u-5v\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = 3u - v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{1}, \\qquad y = u + (\\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{-5})v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{0} \\, .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+(-5)+0 = -4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/example-9508.json" "file_sha256" "03e56da4988b3c55d6fa51e8dc7baa835203339981eb89c541877bebc4fbad27"} {"question" "e-9506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 5u + v - 6, \\qquad y = 2u + 4v\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/f017ccc60a7c1bb9ac09978492c9db217836099d0926ee009ffc44ba827c25d5.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/example-9506.json" "file_sha256" "c40a7537c18977f78785d8d6ea079bb97195701379c2adc66001dd74c7e464e6"} {"question" "e-9506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/514520062cf4564f58267774ba6b50027f9cd27dedfa392cb7038f94580b1e4a.png)\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v-6 \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+2+0 = 3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/example-9506.json" "file_sha256" "c40a7537c18977f78785d8d6ea079bb97195701379c2adc66001dd74c7e464e6"}] "usage" {"q-124285" [] "e-9506" [] "e-9508" [] "q-124284" [] "q-124091" [] "e-9505" [] "q-124253" [] "q-124255" [] "q-124259" [] "q-124291" [] "q-124261" [] "q-124301" [] "q-124247" []} "basis" 2613 "retractions" [[17592186172228 :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n1. $T_{1}: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}v - 7u + 3 \\\\ 3v - u + 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n2. $T_{2}: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}uv + 1 \\\\ u - 2v\\end{bmatrix}$\n3. $T_{3}: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}9u \\\\ u - v\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186172228 :question/answer-fields 17592186168571] [17592186172227 :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$x =-u + av + b, y = 2u - 5v + c$\nis shown below. What is the value of $a + b + c$?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186172230 :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$x = 5u + 3, y = 7v - u$\nis shown below. What is the value of $a + b + c$?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ b & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186171830 :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]$\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]$\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]$"] [17592186171832 :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 3u-v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{a}, \\qquad y = u + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{b}v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{c}\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$"] [17592186171831 :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 5u + v - 6, \\qquad y = 2u + 4v\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$"] [17592186171831 :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v-6 \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+2+0 = 3.\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186168566 17592186168567 17592186168568 17592186168569 17592186168570 17592186168572 17592186168573 17592186168574 17592186168575 17592186168576 17592186168584 17592186168585 17592186168586 17592186168587 17592186168588 17592186295113 17592186295114 17592186295115 17592186295116 17592186295117 17592186295127 17592186295128 17592186295129 17592186295130 17592186295131 17592186295134 17592186295135 17592186295136 17592186295137 17592186295138 17592186295141 17592186295142 17592186295143 17592186295144 17592186295145 17592186295162 17592186295163 17592186295164 17592186295165 17592186295166 17592186295169 17592186295170 17592186295171 17592186295172 17592186295173 17592186295183 17592186295184 17592186295185 17592186295186 17592186295187] "immutable_fields" [[17592186168565 :answer-field/correct] [17592186168565 :answer-field/id] [17592186168565 :answer-field/key] [17592186168565 :answer-field/type] [17592186168571 :answer-field/correct] [17592186168571 :answer-field/id] [17592186168571 :answer-field/key] [17592186168571 :answer-field/type] [17592186168583 :answer-field/correct] [17592186168583 :answer-field/id] [17592186168583 :answer-field/key] [17592186168583 :answer-field/type] [17592186295112 :answer-field/correct] [17592186295112 :answer-field/id] [17592186295112 :answer-field/key] [17592186295112 :answer-field/type] [17592186295126 :answer-field/correct] [17592186295126 :answer-field/id] [17592186295126 :answer-field/key] [17592186295126 :answer-field/type] [17592186295133 :answer-field/correct] [17592186295133 :answer-field/id] [17592186295133 :answer-field/key] [17592186295133 :answer-field/type] [17592186295140 :answer-field/correct] [17592186295140 :answer-field/id] [17592186295140 :answer-field/key] [17592186295140 :answer-field/type] [17592186295161 :answer-field/correct] [17592186295161 :answer-field/id] [17592186295161 :answer-field/key] [17592186295161 :answer-field/typ